# No approval during loops or plans (mandatory)

**Tripping Auto-review / an approval card stops the agent until the developer
comes back.** There is no "try and see." While executing a `/loop`, wake tick,
or any multi-step plan, only use paths that never need approval.

## Forbidden

- Running any command that prompts for approval / Auto-review
- Setting `request_smart_mode_approval` / `requestSmartModeApproval` (that
  *requests* the halt)
- Retrying a blocked command "with approval" — change the approach instead
- Raw `kill` / `pkill` / `killall` (use `.cursor/hooks/kill-test-zombies.sh` only)
- One-shot delayed wake patterns that Auto-review treats as autonomous
  persistence when they would require approval (e.g. bundling
  `sleep N; echo AGENT_LOOP_WAKE_…` into an approval-gated shell)

## Required alternatives (always exist)

| Need | Approval-free path |
|------|--------------------|
| Recurring ticks | Arm a **fixed** `while true; do sleep; echo sentinel; done` **once** at loop start (Cursor `/loop` skill), or rely on an already-running sleeper — do not invent approval-gated re-arms |
| Test leftover cleanup | `.cursor/hooks/kill-test-zombies.sh` only |
| Builds / tests | `taskset` + `nice` + `cargo` as usual |
| Checkpoints | Normal `git commit` on the feature branch per AGENTS.md |
| Docs status lines | Edit tools or skip — never worth an approval risk |
| Anything blocked by Auto-review | Stop that mechanism; pick another path. **Never** wait on the developer |

## Decision rule

If a step might open an approval card, **do not run it** in the loop/plan.
Every necessary action has an approval-free option; use that option.
